  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 407 AM EDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nLatest GFS/EURO and NBM POPs are trending towards lower values \nduring the long term compared to previous runs with potential for a \nmid-week drying trend. One contributing factor will be patches of \nSaharan dust filtering into SoFlo, which will bring increasing \nstability and a stronger mid-lvl cap. This will result in a \nreduction in afternoon convection and less cloud coverage each day. \n\nRain coverage drops to 20-40% each afternoon through Friday with up \nto 50% around the Lake region where the best pool of moisture will \nreside. Then for the weekend, a series of short wave impulses will \ntravel along a deepening trough over the E CONUS and push some of \nthe lingering moisture over northern Florida back into the area. \nThis will result in increasing coverage with a gradient of POPs \nsouth-to-north from 30% around Miami-Dade to 55-60% around the Lake \nregion.  \n\nWith less rain and cloud coverage, expect temperatures to remain \nabove normals, with afternoon highs  temps generally in the low to \nmid 90s and low temps ranging from the middle 70s over inland South \nFL to around 80 closer to the coasts.",
